# Pseudo-cat state preparation circuit (10 qubits)
# Reference [20]: Negrevergne et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 96, 170501 (2006), Fig. 1
# 10 qubits, 54 gates total
#
# Prepares approximate GHZ/cat state: |000...0> + |111...1> (10-qubit)
# NMR gate types: 1=single-qubit (Ry/Rz), 2=two-qubit (ZZ)
# T=1 for Ry(90) or ZZ(90); T=0 for Rz (free gate)
#
# Structure:
#   Phase 1: Initialize superposition (Ry on q0)
#   Phase 2: Linear entanglement chain q0-q1-...-q8-q9 (ZZ gates)
#   Phase 3: Additional long-range entanglement
#   Phase 4: Corrective Ry gates
#   Phase 5: Free Rz frame corrections
#
# NOTE: Exact gate sequence from [20] not available; this is an approximate
#       NMR decomposition of the 10-qubit cat state preparation.
10
# Phase 1: Superposition on q0 (T=1)
1 0 1.0 0
# Phase 2: Linear chain entanglement (ZZ(90), T=1)
2 0 1 1.0 1
2 1 2 1.0 2
2 2 3 1.0 3
2 3 4 1.0 4
2 4 5 1.0 5
2 5 6 1.0 6
2 6 7 1.0 7
2 7 8 1.0 8
2 8 9 1.0 9
# Phase 3: Long-range entanglement (ZZ(90), T=1)
2 0 2 1.0 10
2 2 4 1.0 11
2 4 6 1.0 12
2 6 8 1.0 13
2 0 9 1.0 14
# Phase 4: Corrective Ry rotations (T=1)
1 1 1.0 15
1 2 1.0 15
1 3 1.0 16
1 4 1.0 16
1 5 1.0 17
1 6 1.0 17
1 7 1.0 18
1 8 1.0 18
1 9 1.0 19
# Phase 5: Free Rz frame corrections (T=0)
1 0 0.0 20
1 1 0.0 20
1 2 0.0 20
1 3 0.0 20
1 4 0.0 20
1 5 0.0 21
1 6 0.0 21
1 7 0.0 21
1 8 0.0 21
1 9 0.0 21
1 0 0.0 22
1 1 0.0 22
1 2 0.0 22
1 3 0.0 22
1 4 0.0 22
1 5 0.0 23
1 6 0.0 23
1 7 0.0 23
1 8 0.0 23
1 9 0.0 23
